// ## Reader primitives
//
//   * `mpack_done_array`, `_map`, `_str` and `_bin` (`mpack.h:4150-4185`)
//     are `MPACK_INLINE` calls of `mpack_done_type`. Without tracking, that
//     function is the `MPACK_UNUSED` no-op at `:4139-4142` (amalgamation
//     `:5067-5070`). With tracking, it pops the reader's tracking stack
//     (amalgamation `mpack.c:3848-3851`).
//   * `mpack_reader_destroy(reader)` (`mpack.c:2252-2264`; amalgamation
//     `:2951-2963`) runs `reader->teardown` when one is set, clears it, and
//     returns the reader's error. `mpack_reader_init_data` zeroes the reader
//     and sets no teardown (`:2124-2137`), so in the audited code it frees
//     nothing. The reader object is the caller's own storage (a local) and
//     is not released. `resource_borrowed`. The `mpack_error_t` result is
//     `u32`.
//   * `mpack_expect_nil(reader)` (`:3605-3608`) reads one type byte and sets
//     the error when it is not nil.
//   * `mpack_read_bytes(reader, p, count)` (`:2508-2512`) copies `count`
//     bytes from the reader's data into the caller's buffer `p`
//     (`mpack_read_native`, `mpack.h:4307-4316`). On error or truncated
//     input, it zero-fills `p` (`:2361-2429`).
//   * `mpack_read_cstr(reader, buf, buffer_size, byte_count)` (`:2543-2551`,
//     through `:2523-2541`) copies `byte_count` bytes into `buf` and
//     NUL-terminates it. It sets the error, and writes `buf[0] = 0`, when the
//     string does not fit or holds a NUL byte.
//
// Every pointer is `resource_borrowed`: the reader and the caller's
// destination buffers are written, never freed, stored or returned. Every
// count is `resource_borrowed`. Prototypes `mpack.h:3663`, `:3906`, `:3959`,
// `:4877`. The amalgamation copies of the reader primitives (`:3207`,
// `:3242`, `:4357`) are the same.
//
// NOT CLAIMED: that the reader's data is still live. It points into the
// buffer `mpack_reader_init_data` was given, and no declaration ties the two
// (that initialiser is undeclared). Nor that `count`/`byte_count` fit `p`/`buf`.
//
// LEFT UNDECLARED: `mpack_read_bytes_inplace(reader, count)`
// (`mpack.c:2631-2634` and `mpack_read_bytes_inplace_notrack`) returns a
// pointer into the input buffer the reader references. That buffer is the
// one `mpack_reader_init_data` was given; the reader does not own it.
// `mpack_reader_remaining(reader, data)` (`:2266-2278`) writes that same
// pointer through `data` when `data` is non-NULL. No v1 result or out-slot
// mode is derived from storage a holder references. The derived modes
// (C04.3.1, C04.3.4, C04.16) tie the pointer to the release of a parameter's
// own object, and here that is the wrong object. Both audited calls of
// `mpack_reader_remaining` pass `NULL`, but a literal premise cannot select
// them: `NULL` is a cast (C04.5.1). Follow-up:
// `MPACK-READER-REFERENCED-BUFFER-RESULT`.

extern fn mpack_done_array(reader: ptr<mut, u8>) -> unit
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(reader);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

